  "summary": "The figure is an Arrhenius plot showing the relationship between the natural logarithm of conductivity multiplied by temperature (ln(\u03c3T)) and the inverse of temperature (1000/T) for LLBZT with different compositions (x = 0, 0.05, 0.10, 0.20, 0.30). The data for all compositions shows a linear trend with a negative slope, indicating that conductivity is a thermally activated process. As the value of x increases, the overall conductivity decreases at any given temperature. The slopes of the lines, which relate to the activation energy, appear to be similar for all compositions."
